<section class="block" id="security">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head rv">
      <h2>Trust boundary, declared</h2>
      <p>Albus is explicit about who runs what and what happens when it cannot prove a fact.</p>
    </div>

    <dl class="trust rv">
      <div>
        <dt>Daemon privilege</dt>
        <dd>Management needs root; the runtime drops to a dedicated unprivileged user with a small, named capability set. No ambient root.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>DNSSEC</dt>
        <dd>Chain-validated against an embedded root anchor. An unverifiable answer is SERVFAIL, never cached, never served.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Kill-switch</dt>
        <dd>Plaintext DNS on port 53 is dropped at the firewall unless it targets the local resolver.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Lockdown</dt>
        <dd>If shaping evidence disappears across consecutive windows, the network is locked down until restart. Doubt becomes refusal.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Update model</dt>
        <dd>Reload eBPF maps and configuration over SIGHUP without restarting or dropping active flows.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .trust {
    margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .trust > div {
    padding: 22px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr; gap: 24px; align-items: baseline;
  }
  .trust dt { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .trust dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .trust { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .trust > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>
